  "decision": "Approved",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be commenced before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.<br>",
    "<p>The development hereby approved shall only be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:</p><ul><li>Planning Statement (Received: 06/07/2024)</li><li>Site Location Plan (dated: May 2022)</li><li>Existing and Proposed Loft Plan (drawing number: S003, dated: June 2024)&nbsp;</li><li>Existing and Proposed Roof Plan (drawing number: S004, dated: June 2024)&nbsp;</li><li>Existing and Proposed Side Elevations (drawing number: S006, dated: June 2024)&nbsp;</li><li>Existing and Proposed Front and Rear Elevations (drawing number: S005, dated: June 2024)&nbsp;</li><li>Proposed Ground Floor Plan (drawing number: P001, dated: June 2024)&nbsp;</li><li>Proposed First Floor Plan&nbsp;(drawing number: P002, dated: June 2024)&nbsp;</li><li>Proposed Block Plan (drawing number: P.BP,&nbsp; dated: June 2024)&nbsp;</li><li>Parking Stress Survey (dated 24/06/2024)</li></ul><p>No other drawings or documents apply.</p>",
    "Care Home Capacity&nbsp;The care home hereby approved shall be occupied by no more than 3 children and 2 carers at any one time without prior permission of the Local Planning Authority.&nbsp;",
    "Ancillary Outbuilding&nbsp;The existing outbuilding shall not be occupied or used at any\r\ntime other than for purposes ancillary to the use of the care home hereby\r\napproved, and shall not be used as additional residential accommodation .&nbsp;",
    "Cycle Parking&nbsp;a)\tPrior to first use of the site details of all cycle storage including the design, quantum and location shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. All cycle storage shall be designed in accordance with the London Cycle Design Standards.&nbsp;b)\tThe approved cycle storage shall be implemented and thereafter maintained for the lifetime of the development.&nbsp;",
    "Sound Insulation Scheme. A scheme for the sound insulation of the party wall between the proposed development and the structurally adjoining noise sensitive property shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the LPA. The scheme approved by the LPA shall be fully implemented in accordance with the approved details before the use, hereby permitted, commences.The works and scheme shall thereafter be retained in accordance with the approved details. No alteration to the separating partition which undermines the sound insulation integrity shall be undertaken without the grant of further specific consent of the LPA."
  ],
